Subject: [PATCH 0/4] Lenovo ThinkSmart View front camera (Samsung S5KC505A)

This series enables the front camera of the Lenovo ThinkSmart View
(CD-18781Y, APQ8053): a Samsung S5KC505A 5 MP raw sensor on CSIPHY0.

Patch 1 fixes CAMSS on MSM8953 in general: the CSIPHY timer clock at
100 MHz (GPLL0_EARLY_DIV) never turns on, so no CSIPHY could be powered
up. Using the GPLL0-derived 200/266.67 MHz rates fixes it.

Patches 2-3 add a binding and a driver for the S5KC505A. There is no
public datasheet; the register settings come from the sensor
configuration in the device's Android firmware.

Patch 4 describes the camera in the ThinkSmart View device tree.

Tested on the ThinkSmart View: RAW10 capture with v4l2-ctl through
csiphy0 -> csid0 -> ispif0 -> vfe0_rdi0, and with libcamera (simple
pipeline + software ISP, with a matching S5KC505A camera sensor helper
sent to libcamera-devel separately).

